    "body": "Thanks for taking a look @davidwendt, @ttnghia. It doesn't make a lot of sense to run out of memory with 48GB for ~5GB input for a simple sum. Looking with @jlowe and @nvdbaranec the second overflow in `gather` is likely due to the `size_type` usage in `cudf::distance`, would that make sense?\r\n\r\nThe main thing is not having the overflow, if there is another overflow via the `gather` we should fix it as well.",
